/Users/mindlace/Projects/sfhousing/.claude/worktrees/incremental-game/.superpowers/superconductor/incremental-game/rulings/game-core-8.md

The ruling takes option 1. The store's interface (row G2) gains `beforeLeave(fn)`, and it is the one interface change in this ruling:
- **Paint and `SimPage` register their autosave's flush** with it when they mount, and remove it when they unmount.
- **The store runs those flushes first** on New game, switching to another game, Remix and deleting the current game. They run before the store reads or writes the saved plan or policy, so an edit still inside the 500 ms autosave delay is saved into the old game.
- **`touched()` is ignored after such a change succeeds.** The page reloads next, and a write it makes while unloading must not count as a change to the new game.

I updated row G2 in the design doc and in the five specs that copy it: contracts, game-core, game-save, game-shell and game-sim. I also added the store's rules and tests to game-core, and the hook registration and a test to game-shell and game-sim. Each of those four running units only needs a clarification; no plan task is cut back. The contracts stub that's already merged doesn't have `beforeLeave`; game-core adds it when it writes the real store.

